r3 runtime (390x844, f3d3614 web build): after the landing→board hook put the world camera exactly on the
board camera's pose (gap view 1.2e-6°, FOV 0, position 0), WorldFlow.enterLevel still played the generic
island push-in (ENTER_LEVEL_SHOT_S 0.78 s: 2.6 m dolly, FOV 57.35→51.35), then the board's
LakesideBackgroundCamera took over at the pre-push pose: a visible 2.6 m / 6° jump back at the swap.

- WorldFlowComponent: one-shot holdEnterLevel(on). When set, playEnterLevel holds the frame for the same
  ENTER_LEVEL_SHOT_S (board reveal timing unchanged) and writes no camera.
- WorldNativeComposition: set only in the lakeside branch after the hook landed (not on the fallback),
  cleared in finally after enterLevel. Other regions/levels keep the push-in.
- test-lakeside-landing-hook: wiring/one-shot contract check.
